  32:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (#) Declare a SAI_HandleTypeDef handle structure (eg. SAI_HandleTypeDef hsai).
  33:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (#) Initialize the SAI low level resources by implementing the HAL_SAI_MspInit() API:
  34:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) Enable the SAI interface clock.
  35:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) SAI pins configuration:
  36:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the SAI GPIOs.
  37:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure these SAI pins as alternate function pull-up.
  38:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process (HAL_SAI_Transmit_IT()
  39:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****              and HAL_SAI_Receive_IT() APIs):
  40:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the SAI interrupt priority.
  41:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC SAI IRQ handle.
  42:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  43:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) DMA Configuration if you need to use DMA process (HAL_SAI_Transmit_DMA()
  44:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****              and HAL_SAI_Receive_DMA() APIs):
  45:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Declare a DMA handle structure for the Tx/Rx stream.
  46:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Enable the DMAx interface clock.
  47:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the declared DMA handle structure with the required Tx/Rx parameters.
  48:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the DMA Tx/Rx Stream.
  49:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Associate the initialized DMA handle to the SAI DMA Tx/Rx handle.
  50:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****             (+++) Configure the priority and enable the NVIC for the transfer complete interrupt on
  51:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****                 DMA Tx/Rx Stream.
  52:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  53:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (#) The initialization can be done by two ways
  54:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) Expert mode : Initialize the structures Init, FrameInit and SlotInit and call HAL_SAI_
  55:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (##) Simplified mode : Initialize the high part of Init Structure and call HAL_SAI_InitProt
  56:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  57:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  58:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) The specific SAI interrupts (FIFO request and Overrun underrun interrupt)
  59:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         will be managed using the macros __HAL_SAI_ENABLE_IT() and __HAL_SAI_DISABLE_IT()
  60:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         inside the transmit and receive process.
  61:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  62:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) Make sure that either:
  63:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI1CLK output is configured or
  64:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI2CLK output is configured or
  65:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI3CLK output is configured or
  66:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI4ACLK output is configured or
  67:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) PLLSAI4BCLK output is configured or
  68:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) External clock source is configured after setting correctly
  69:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****              the define constant EXTERNAL_CLOCK_VALUE in the stm32h7xx_hal_conf.h file.
  70:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  71:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  72:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) In master Tx mode: enabling the audio block immediately generates the bit clock
  73:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         for the external slaves even if there is no data in the FIFO, However FS signal
  74:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         generation is conditioned by the presence of data in the FIFO.
  75:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  76:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  77:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) In master Rx mode: enabling the audio block immediately generates the bit clock
  78:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         and FS signal for the external slaves.
  79:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  80:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  81:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) It is mandatory to respect the following conditions in order to avoid bad SAI behavior:
  82:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) First bit Offset <= (SLOT size - Data size)
  83:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) Data size <= SLOT size
  84:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) Number of SLOT x SLOT size = Frame length
  85:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         (+@) The number of slots should be even when SAI_FS_CHANNEL_IDENTIFICATION is selected.
  86:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  87:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  88:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     (@) PDM interface can be activated through HAL_SAI_Init function.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\oleg\AppData\Local\Temp\cc7eBfYh.s 			page 3


  89:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         Please note that PDM interface is only available for SAI1 or SAI4 sub-block A.
  90:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****         PDM microphone delays can be tuned with HAL_SAIEx_ConfigPdmMicDelay function.
  91:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  92:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****   [..]
  93:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Three operation modes are available within this driver :
  94:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
  95:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** Polling mode IO operation ***
  96:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     =================================
  97:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
  98:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Send an amount of data in blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Transmit()
  99:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Receive an amount of data in blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Receive()
 100:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 101:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** Interrupt mode IO operation ***
 102:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     ===================================
 103:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 104:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Send an amount of data in non-blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Transmit_IT()
 105:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At transmission end of transfer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 106:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback()
 107:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Receive an amount of data in non-blocking mode using HAL_SAI_Receive_IT()
 108:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At reception end of transfer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 109:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback()
 110:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) In case of flag error, HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback() function is executed and user can
 111:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback()
 112:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 113:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** DMA mode IO operation ***
 114:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     =============================
 115:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 116:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Send an amount of data in non-blocking mode (DMA) using HAL_SAI_Transmit_DMA()
 117:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At transmission end of transfer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 118:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_TxCpltCallback()
 119:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Receive an amount of data in non-blocking mode (DMA) using HAL_SAI_Receive_DMA()
 120:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) At reception end of transfer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback() is executed and user can
 121:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback()
 122:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) In case of flag error, HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback() function is executed and user can
 123:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****           add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback()
 124:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Pause the DMA Transfer using HAL_SAI_DMAPause()
 125:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Resume the DMA Transfer using HAL_SAI_DMAResume()
 126:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) Stop the DMA Transfer using HAL_SAI_DMAStop()
 127:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
