 145:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) __HAL_SAI_ENABLE(): Enable the SAI peripheral
ARM GAS  C:\Users\oleg\AppData\Local\Temp\cc7eBfYh.s 			page 4


 146:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) __HAL_SAI_DISABLE(): Disable the SAI peripheral
 147:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) __HAL_SAI_ENABLE_IT(): Enable the specified SAI interrupts
 148:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) __HAL_SAI_DISABLE_IT(): Disable the specified SAI interrupts
 149:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) __HAL_SAI_GET_IT_SOURCE(): Check if the specified SAI interrupt source is
 150:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****           enabled or disabled
 151:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) __HAL_SAI_GET_FLAG(): Check whether the specified SAI flag is set or not
 152:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 153:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     *** Callback registration ***
 154:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     =============================
 155:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 156:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     The compilation define USE_HAL_SAI_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 157:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 158:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Use functions HAL_SAI_RegisterCallback() to register a user callback.
 159:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 160:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 161:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Function HAL_SAI_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 162:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback     : SAI receive complete.
 163:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxHalfCpltCallback : SAI receive half complete.
 164:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback     : SAI transmit complete.
 165:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxHalfCpltCallback : SAI transmit half complete.
 166:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback      : SAI error.
 167:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SAI MspInit.
 168:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SAI MspDeInit.
 169:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 170:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the callback ID
 171:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
 172:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 173:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 174:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Use function HAL_SAI_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 175:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     weak function.
 176:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     HAL_SAI_UnRegisterCallback() takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 177:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     and the callback ID.
 178:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 179:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 180:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxCpltCallback     : SAI receive complete.
 181:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) RxHalfCpltCallback : SAI receive half complete.
 182:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxCpltCallback     : SAI transmit complete.
 183:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) TxHalfCpltCallback : SAI transmit half complete.
 184:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) ErrorCallback      : SAI error.
 185:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspInitCallback    : SAI MspInit.
 186:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****       (+) MspDeInitCallback  : SAI MspDeInit.
 187:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 188:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 189:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     By default, after the HAL_SAI_Init and if the state is HAL_SAI_STATE_RESET
 190:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     all callbacks are reset to the corresponding legacy weak functions:
 191:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     examples HAL_SAI_RxCpltCallback(), HAL_SAI_ErrorCallback().
 192:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit callbacks that are respectively
 193:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_SAI_Init
 194:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     and HAL_SAI_DeInit only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 195:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_SAI_Init and HAL_SAI_DeInit
 196:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand).
 197:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c **** 
 198:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     [..]
 199:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in READY state only.
 200:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     Exception done for MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks that can be registered/unregistered
 201:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     in READY or RESET state, thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used
 202:../../Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_sai.c ****     during the Init/DeInit.
